 A saffron quotation is easier to compare when three questions stay separate: what material is being supplied, what its reported quality measurements mean, and which substitutions the laboratory actually looked for. Research on saffron powders and filaments shows why one attractive result cannot close all three questions.[1][2]
 
-For buyers, the useful conclusion is not “order every available test.” It is to match the evidence to the purchase: dried stigmas, milled stigmas or a processed extract, with any carrier explicitly declared. The procurement framework below is our interpretation of the research, not a validated release specification or a claim about a particular supplier.
